operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{cos}^{2}⁡t+4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{cos}^{2}⁡t+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=4x-2y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =4(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-2(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(4x-2y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343283 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343284 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343285 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343286 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343287 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1041 "selection" 13194139535314 true] [17592186343282 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343285 131941395353